WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.360
Scott Shawyer has decided not to start the route du Rhum after sea sickness cut short his qualifying attempt in the English Channel. This is Offshore North Episode 9. Every four years, a small number of sailors set out alone on the hardest race in the sport. And one Canadian is working toward becoming the first to finish it. On the Canadian boat as of October 12, 2026, the team's YB tracker shows Emira for alongside in Gossport UK in Port Smith Harbor. Canada Ocean Racing posted on 8 October that Scott Shawyer will not compete in this year's route du Rhum.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.240
The summer training block in Canada gave him time to learn the boat systems, but an unexpected

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.380
energy systems issue on the return delivery in a very short qualification window complicated

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.220
the final steps.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.980
During the recent qualifying attempt, C sickness struck quickly while he worked on the computer

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.340
systems, and in the busy waters of the English channel he turned back after weighing the risks.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.940
The post explains that getting a mirror forward to Canada for a summer of training was a major

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.360
project that gave Scott valuable time on board to learn how the boat performs, understand

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:03.220
her systems and build muscle memory. While in Canada, the team identified improvements to the boat

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.980
and her systems. The plan was to return to the UK, complete the most important work, and then

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.040
set off on the qualifying passage for November's route to rum, which was to be his first solo race on

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.060
Amira 4. On the attempt, sea sickness hit fast while trying to get the computer systems working,

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.620
and in the busy channel waters he had to assess the risks and turn back. The post adds that Scott spent

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.600
many days on the water, learning sales, rigging, foils, electrical systems, hydrogenerators,

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.580
solar, and autopilot overlays system by system. He notes that on two heavy days his triceps seized

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.720
on the grinder, which he traces to pushing rather than pulling because of a shoulder injury,

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.200
and to not drinking enough water with electrolytes. He has not yet sailed in Mirafor in the open oceans

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.220
waves and swell, and says he needs to remain humble. The support team named includes Martin,

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:56.300
M.SQA, Gabi Bukau, Clovis Gautier, Julina Biyat, Alberto Zaccarria, Alan Roberts on

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.520
rooting and autopilot, and Nick Maloney as sailing coach. That choice keeps the first solo race on

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.620
Amira 4 for a later date and shifts the immediate focus to whatever qualifying path remains open before

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.980
the 2028 Vendée Globe. The decision means the campaign's next steps will focus on completing

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.620
the work identified during the Canadian summer and preparing for future qualifying opportunities

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:22.240
that count toward the 2028 start. Every solo race finished on Emura for both banks,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.440
Globe Series points, and can tick the solo qualifier box under the published outline.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.920
The decision at C on incomplete information at 3 in the morning is the same trade-off

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.540
of pilot faces when roading across the North Atlantic. Now the fleet.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:40.260
Orelian Ducrose announced on 8 October that he has bought the 2012 Owen Clark design previously

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:46.520
owned by Scott Shire, the boat that raced as Axiona and capsized in the 2012-13 Vendée

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.960
globe after losing its keel.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:53.760
Ducrose plans to campaign it as Ocean Peak, pairing the 2028 Vendée Globe with an attempt

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.560
to climb 82 Alpine peaks over 4,000 meters.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.800
The move adds another Class 40 skipper to the IMLK ranks at a time when several established

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.800
names have stepped back.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.620
The article notes that since the last Vendée Globe, the class has welcomed new skippers most

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:16.080
from Class 40, including Pierre-Louis Atwell with Resilient, Robin Morey with Respire, William

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:16.900
Baptiste Deremi.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.320
Ducrose, 44, from Chamonix, chose this boat after looking at others, including Violet

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.080
Duranges and Guirex Sudeis because it hasn't completed five round the world races, giving

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:31.020
it a different profile for his dual passion project combining sailing and mountaineering.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.220
He told sailors the acquisition lets him put a foot in the door and encourage partners

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.000
to come on board.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:41.180
Porto will become the global headquarters of the Ocean Race from 2028 under a long-term

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:47.580
agreement that also brings the start of the 2030, 2034, and 2038 additions to the city.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.820
Plus at least six additions of the ocean race Europe to Portugal.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.120
The deal runs through 2040 and includes a new operational base and museum on the waterfront.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.780
The partnership aims to strengthen Portugal's position as a destination for major international

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.460
sporting events while establishing Porto as a leading European hub for offshore sailing.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.480
Race Chairman Richard Briseus said the city shares the purpose of inspiring the world to achieve

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.920
the extraordinary, and the agreement will connect Porto with coastal communities across Portugal,

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:20.260
supporting international sailing events, ocean science, education, and sustainability initiatives.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.480
A historic waterfront building near Porto City Park will be transformed into the operational headquarters

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:31.580
with public and educational activities planned from 2028. Alexia Barrier told Boiles,

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:37.540
a Boile A, that sailing the IMOCA solo for the first time in the route to Rome will be a new exercise

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.500
after years of crude racing. The video interview highlights her preparation for the solo challenge

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:49.000
on the machine in the upcoming transatlantic event. Time for plain sailing. An IMOCA 60 carries two

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.060
very different foil systems. Dagger boards are vertical blades that slide up and down to reduce leeway

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:59.120
and add lift when the boat heals. They work in a wide range of conditions and are simpler to manage.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.580
True foils are L-shaped or T-shaped appendages that generate enough upward force to lift the entire

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.600
hull clear of the water once the boat reaches a certain speed.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.020
On a foiling IMOCA, the transition happens around 12-15 knots.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.700
Above that, the drag drops sharply and the boat can sustain 30-plus knots for hours.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.720
The trade-off is that a foil boat is more sensitive to setup and more vulnerable if one foil

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:26.120
is damaged, which is why some teams still choose dagger boards for their first seasons on the

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:26.340
class.

